# Keys of the device tree list in the initramfs (boot-dtb-select D7), read by lume-bootsel
# from /etc/bootsel-keys. <role>=<key>[,<key>...], with names of linux/input-event-codes.h
# or numbers. select: held at power on, opens the list.
#
# Proof 1.3 (2026-11-16, boots 122 to 126): Vol- (LRADC ~0xC) falls between the U-Boot
# ranges and boots normally, so it opens the list as on the R36S; Vol+ held at power on
# (~0x6, the fastboot range 0x2-0x8) takes the factory U-Boot to the Allwinner USB mode
# (1f3a:efe8, no screen) and must never be the select key; Start, Select and A (the gamepad
# MCU) are not seen by the U-Boot. A held Vol- needs kernel/patches/0034 (LRADC "already
# hold").
# Volume keys: LRADC (built in, ready early); D-pad and A: the gamepad MCU (BTN_SOUTH is
# BTN_A, the A button of the GA36 driver).
select=KEY_VOLUMEDOWN
up=BTN_DPAD_UP,KEY_VOLUMEUP
down=BTN_DPAD_DOWN,KEY_VOLUMEDOWN
ok=BTN_SOUTH
